<%# locals: (provisions:, type:, person:) %>
<%# The first step of the provision dialog the BMID manage grid opens from a
    meals or showers cell: everything that cell's label is describing, so an
    admin can pick the pass they meant -- or add another.

    A person can hold two usable passes of one type (an earned one and an
    allocated one, or an earned one that was banked and came back into play
    because they hold an allocated one). The cell shows the union, so the table
    carries the source year, the expiry, the status, and earned-or-allocated:
    what it takes to tell two of them apart.

    Picking one swaps this frame for the record form; saving there closes the
    dialog and redraws the row's two cells. %>
<%= modal id: "bmid-provision-modal", size: :xl, close_button: false do |m| %>
  <%= m.title do %>
    <%= bmid_provision_noun(type).titleize %> &mdash; <%= person.callsign %>
  <% end %>
  <%= m.body do %>
    <p class="mb-3 text-body">
      Meals and showers are printed from the person's provisions, so anything you change
      here saves on its own, right away. It does not touch the badge, and it does not join
      the badge changes you have in progress.
    </p>

    <%= render "common/provisions/list",
               provisions: provisions,
               ref_path: ->(provision) { edit_bmid_provision_path(provision, provision_context) },
               empty_message: "No #{bmid_provision_noun(type)} on file for #{person.callsign}.",
               frame: "modal",
               action_label: "Edit" %>

    <div class="mt-4">
      <%= button_row do %>
        <%= button_link bmid_provision_add_label(type), :primary,
                        new_bmid_provision_path(provision_context.merge(type:)),
                        icon: "plus", icon_type: :solid,
                        data: { turbo_frame: "modal" } %>
        <%= modal_close_button "Close" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
